From e89970e42e13c65ac4f08c7dd0a800b75714ae8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:55:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] upstream sync gate: trust only the real upstream,
 refuse ship-tool faults, drop HERMES_UPSTREAM_SYNC_IMPL_TASK

Follow-up to the independent review (t_01a1d6bd2176a195) of PR #2671, the fork-authored-sync review gate.
Card t_01a1d6cc89d51f84.

1. Possible fail-open: classify() excluded `^upstream/main` from whatever the local `upstream` remote/ref
   held. An `upstream` remote pointing at a fork that holds the conflict-resolution merge (or a local
   upstream/main moved onto fork commits) hid the fork-authored content and the sync landed as mechanical.
   verified_upstream() now requires every configured `remote.upstream.url` to name
   github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent (https / git@ / ssh forms, case-insensitive) and re-fetches
   upstream/main from it before classifying; anything else is a ClassifyError -> REFUSED (land and
   --classify alike).
2. A ship-tool exception other than ReviewRefused / ReviewCIStopped / SharedQuotaBrake (or any fault while
   loading the tool) escaped advance() as a traceback. ShipReview.check now turns it into ReviewUnavailable
   ("review gate failed: <Type>: <message>"), which the gate prints as REFUSED; nothing merges.
3. HERMES_UPSTREAM_SYNC_IMPL_TASK duplicated --impl-task (root AGENTS.md: no new HERMES_* env vars). Removed;
   --impl-task is the only source (the ship tool already excludes $HERMES_KANBAN_TASK's sessions itself).
   No callers used it. .github/LANDING.md documents the upstream URL rule and --impl-task.

Test fixtures: make_world configures `upstream` as https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent.git with an
insteadOf to the local bare remote, so every existing gate test runs through the real URL check.

New tests (tests/scripts/ci/test_upstream_sync_review.py) and their mutants (each fix reverted, the named
test fails; restored, all 16 pass):
- M1 URL check removed      -> test_an_upstream_remote_that_is_not_the_real_upstream_refuses[both] FAIL
                               (gate returned LANDED: the fail-open)
- M1 re-fetch removed       -> test_a_local_upstream_ref_moved_onto_fork_commits_is_refetched FAIL (LANDED)
- M2 catch-all removed      -> test_an_unexpected_ship_tool_error_refuses_naming_it FAIL (RuntimeError escapes)
- M3 env read restored      -> test_impl_task_comes_from_the_flag_only FAIL ('t_from_env' == '')

Ran: scripts/run_tests.sh on all six tests/scripts/ci/test_upstream_sync*.py files: 149 passed;
scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks ok.
